A||||17||Smokin' GT||Greetings from the peanut gallery||||2||
Z||000000||Smokin' GT||10-10-2001||02:21 AM||||Hi guys, my name is Joel and I justed wanted to say what's up.  I'm eighteen and i just bought a couple months ago a very clean '87 GT.  I had been searching for something fast and sporty for quite a while, looking into cars like the RX7s, Supras, 3000GTs, MR2s...etc and one day I saw this gorgeous looking car drive by and I thought, "Holy **** , what kind of car was that!"  So after some in-depth research I found this was the epic "Pontiac Fiero GT" *and the light shined down from the heavens*  So among my considerations for buying a car was basically that it had to perform but still had to look cool (seriously folks, it's like, I don't know about you, but no matter how cool ugly girls are, if you're not attracted it doesn't work, the same thing goes for me and monte carlos SS or not)...  So the whole mid-engine thing was awesome, I'm more into style than muscle, I've got a friend with an extremely fast Trans Am GTA, the car's fast. but the guy's an ******* , I don't know if that has to do with anything... <P>But anyways guys, I love my car.  The lack of body roll and handling is a blessing... it performs great, I was smokin' a friend with a V6 camaro at every stoplight, just a great car.  Although, the engine has got to be one of the biggest bitches to work on.  My dad and I recently pulled the engine in order to put new rod and main bearings, timing chain set, and a new clutch...  Now I don't know how many of you guy have pulled the cradle out, but let's just say it doesn't exactly appeal to me as something I want to do again in the near future!  But it's a great car, I plan on getting the west coast fiero adapted flowmaster, intake, big bore throttle body... all that fun stuff, if you guys have any simple mods I'd love to hear it...  I just wanted to introduce myself to all of you, thanks for your time.<P>------------------<BR>-87 Bright Blue Metallic GT-<BR>          -Joel||||reg||2
Z||000001||My7Fieros||10-10-2001||02:33 AM||||Welcome to the forum! Sounds like you got yourself a nice GT. You've come to the right place for Fiero everything! Check it out dailey (or like most of us, several times a day)...you'll grow just as addicted to this forum as you will to your Fiero. Once again, WELCOME!<P>------------------<BR><FONT SIZE="3"><FONT COLOR="blue"><B><I>My 7 Fieros</FONT></FONT></B></I>||||reg||14
Z||000002||Hippocrat||10-10-2001||02:44 AM||||Yes Welcome..<P>Bye the way if you just doing engine work?<P>I personally find it easier to just pull the motor out through the top. ||||reg||14
Z||000003||Smokin' GT||10-10-2001||02:57 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Hippocrat:<BR><B>Yes Welcome..<P>Bye the way if you just doing engine work?<P>I personally find it easier to just pull the motor out through the top. </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Right, but I had to do the clutch also, so the tranny had to come off too, I dunno it might have worked good that way, the way we did it was upon the advice of my neighbor, he was working GM when they first came out and the many recalls were going on... would the tranny come out with the engine out the top? ||||reg||1
Z||000004||My7Fieros||10-10-2001||03:00 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Hippocrat:<BR><B>Yes Welcome..<P>Bye the way if you just doing engine work?<P>I personally find it easier to just pull the motor out through the top. </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><BR>Hippocrat is one out of maybe 4 people on here that find it "easier" to pull the engine through the top...for a Fiero "newbie" as yourself, I wouldnt recomend it.....drop the cradle out the bottom. (Or I guess whatever works for you)<P><P>------------------<BR><FONT SIZE="3"><FONT COLOR="blue"><B><I>My 7 Fieros</FONT></FONT></B></I>||||reg||4
Z||000005||Hippocrat||10-10-2001||03:16 AM||||tis true pretty much new with these fiero gadgets.. <BR>(1st time buyer.. long time admirer)<P>That post was made based on only 4 changes (motor only not tranny) <P>1st through the top. <BR>2nd dropped the cradle.<P>3rd and 4th.. decided Id rather pull through the top. <P>Mind you mines a 4 banger so I probably got a little more room to play with. But as long as I have a 4 in there mine will be coming through the top.<BR>just old fashioned I guess.<P>Everyone I know with a Fiero (the whole whopping three of them) would probably agree dropping the cradle is easier. Perhaps one day I too will see the light. <p>[This message has been edited by Hippocrat (edited 10-10-2001).]||||reg||1
